\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The coupled chain’s quantum force and non-Gaussian vacuum}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{Return to the quartic chain of \ref{fdip-00GV}, with #{s\ge2},
#{c,m>0}, free endpoints and some #{\lambda_v>0}.
Its Hilbert space is #{L^2(\mathbb R^s)}, and \ref{fdip-00H2},
\ref{fdip-00H3} and \ref{fdip-00H6} give its self-adjoint
Hamiltonian, compact resolvent, finite thermal trace and unique
positive vacuum. On the transported test domains of
\ref{fdip-00HA}, at each fixed time the field equations are
##{\begin{aligned}
\frac{\extd}{\extd t}\Phi_v(t)&=\Pi_v(t),\\
\frac{\extd}{\extd t}\Pi_v(t)&=-m^2\Phi_v(t)
 -c\sum_{w:\,|w-v|=1}(\Phi_v(t)-\Phi_w(t))
 -\frac{\lambda_v}{6}\Phi_v(t)^3.
\end{aligned}}
The neighbor sum has one term at an endpoint and two in the
interior. The spatial coupling and the nonlinear quantum force
therefore coexist for arbitrarily many finite sites.}

\p{The positive vacuum cannot be Gaussian. A Gaussian candidate
would have the form
#{\psi(q)=C\exp(-(q-u)^TA(q-u)/2)} with #{A} real positive
definite. Substitution into the Schrödinger expression gives
##{\frac{H\psi}{\psi}
 =\frac{\traceA}{2}-\frac{|A(q-u)|^2}{2}
  +\frac{q^TKq}{2}+\sum_v\frac{\lambda_vq_v^4}{24}.}
The derivative and quadratic terms have degree at most two.
The nonzero quartic polynomial cannot cancel, so this ratio cannot
be the constant #{E_0}. The vacuum position law #{\psi_0^2\extd q}
is also non-Gaussian: the positive square root of a nondegenerate
Gaussian density has the excluded form. A degenerate Gaussian
law cannot have the everywhere positive density supplied by
\ref{fdip-00H6}.}

\p{When all #{\lambda_v=0}, the obstruction disappears and the
coupled Gaussian oscillator is recovered. For nonzero quartic
coupling, the construction gives a bosonic quantum scalar field
with finite spatial volume and continuous time. Its vacuum and
thermal states are distinct, and no infinite-volume or relativistic
continuum reconstruction follows from the finite Hamiltonian alone.}
